@FG-M1-e3684cb036 OVERMERGE_FACET conf=M om=COMPOUND_NEEDS_OVERLAY cls=SUBCLAUSE
why: S1 and S2 are right. The claim also says project files or references changed without a recognized command are reported for confirmation of the owning workflow, and no stored subclause carries that. It is a different action with a different effect: a reminder after the fact, not a denial. Proposed as a local overlay; the group is not split.
q: .claude/hooks/post-tool-use.js:165-165 | Confirm the owning workflow was applied
set subclauses_add=[{"subclause_id":"AUD-S3","classification":"EXTRA_WORKFLOW","modality":"DEFAULT","text":"Project files or references changed, removed or moved without a recognized command are reported, and the agent is asked to confirm the owning workflow was applied. A branch switch needs no workflow.","extra_fragment":"Post-hoc confirmation reminder for project-file changes outside a recognized command.","extra_fragment_kind":"EXTRA_WORKFLOW","distinguishing_scenario":"A csproj is edited directly: no canonical policy asks for a confirmation of the workflow; the hook prompts it.","canonical_coverage":[]}]
